WEBVTT

00:06:25.996 --> 00:06:30.496
I work at a nearby prison, Hamilton
Correctional Institution.

00:06:30.788 --> 00:06:32.621
Aaron now helps people navigate one of

00:06:32.621 --> 00:06:35.454
the biggest headwinds imaginable
time in prison.

00:06:35.954 --> 00:06:39.788
What Aaron's learned about how formerly
incarcerated people re-enter society

00:06:39.996 --> 00:06:42.746
has implications for adapting
to all kinds of turbulence,

00:06:43.038 --> 00:06:46.954
from being downsized to being demoted
to having a gap on your resume.

00:06:47.746 --> 00:06:50.954
People who have spent time in prison faced
major obstacles when they're trying

00:06:50.954 --> 00:06:55.079
to land a job. Employers are often
hesitant to give them an opportunity.

00:06:55.579 --> 00:07:00.163
If they look you up and they find out
you are really into some bad stuff,